Blood compatibility of the bilayer scaffolds was assessed using a hemolysis assay. A scaffold with a diameter of 1 cm was incubated with a mixture of 0.2 mL fresh anticoagulated blood and 5 mL of 0.9% NaCl at 37 °C for 1 h. After incubation, the mixture was centrifuged at 1000 rpm for 10 min. Then, 100 μL of the supernatant was transferred to a 96-well plate, and absorbance at 450 nm was measured. The negative control consisted of fresh anticoagulated blood and 0.9% NaCl without scaffolds, while the positive control contained fresh anticoagulated blood and 1% Triton X-100 in 0.9% NaCl without scaffolds. The test was performed in triplicate. The percentage of hemolysis was calculated as described below (6):6\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
